 ## Overview
-FluidX12 is a real-time volume rendering pipeline that simulates smoke using an Eulerian grid method to solve the Navier-Stokes equations [S1, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself by integrating viewport-resolution independent anti-aliased ray marching on interior faces in cube-map space, allowing for high-quality volumetric rendering at interactive frame rates [S1, unofficial]. Unlike standard fluid solvers that output static data, this pipeline couples the simulation state directly with a specialized ray-marching renderer that supports both 2D and 3D domains.
